<h2 id="jenny" class="reveal">Jenny</h2>
<p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#5A9EAD;" class="reveal">Therapeutic Yoga, Restorative Yoga &amp; Sound Healing</p>

<div style="text-align:center;" class="reveal">
  <img src="/img/Jsq.jpg" alt="Jenny" class="practitioner-photo">
</div>

<p class="reveal">Jenny is a Registered Yoga Teacher (RYT) with Yoga Alliance, bringing over a decade of dedicated experience in yoga practice and teaching, with particular expertise in Therapeutic Yoga and Restorative Yoga. She has been teaching Yoga at UNI Yoga Academy at senior tutor level in Vietnam, leading and contributing to numerous 200-hour and 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training programmes, mentoring and supporting the next generation of Yoga teachers. Restorative Yoga is a core component of her curriculum, reflecting her commitment to practices that support deep healing and recovery.</p>

<p class="reveal">In recent years, Jenny has expanded her practice into Sound Healing, completing extensive training in therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation. She integrates meridian sound healing, therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation into her classes to support deep relaxation, energetic balance and holistic healing.</p>

<p class="reveal">Known for her calm presence and authentic approach, Jenny creates a grounded and supportive space where students can slow down, reconnect with their bodies and cultivate deeper awareness. Her work bridges traditional yogic wisdom with therapeutic practice, and her understanding of how sound, breath and movement interact along the body's energy pathways informs every class she teaches.</p>

<h3 class="reveal" id="ytt-200hr">200-Hour Online Yoga Teacher Training</h3>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>A comprehensive foundational programme leading to RYT-200 certification with Yoga Alliance. Delivered online and suitable for those who want to begin teaching yoga, as well as dedicated practitioners who wish to deepen their understanding of the practice and its philosophy.</p>
</div>

<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Asana technique, alignment and teaching methodology</li>
<li>Anatomy and physiology relevant to yoga practice</li>
<li>Pranayama, meditation and subtle energy practices</li>
<li>Yoga philosophy and history</li>
<li>Therapeutic and Restorative Yoga elements</li>
<li>Teaching practicum with guided feedback</li>
<li>Ethics and the foundations of teaching</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="reveal" id="ytt-500hr">500-Hour Online Yoga Teacher Training</h3>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>An advanced programme building on the 200-hour foundation, designed for teachers who want to refine their skills, broaden their knowledge and deepen their practice. Leads to RYT-500 certification with Yoga Alliance.</p>
</div>

<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Advanced asana, alignment and adjustment techniques</li>
<li>Deeper exploration of yoga philosophy and classical texts</li>
<li>Therapeutic and Restorative Yoga as core components</li>
<li>Advanced pranayama and subtle energy practices</li>
<li>Working with specific conditions and individual student needs</li>
<li>Advanced teaching methodology and class design</li>
<li>Mentored teaching practice</li>
</ul>

<p class="reveal">Prerequisite: RYT-200 certification or equivalent training.</p>

<h3 class="reveal" id="yin-yoga-monthly">Online Monthly Yin Yoga Series</h3>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>A monthly online Yin Yoga programme - a slow, meditative practice of long-held postures that work deep into the connective tissue and along the body's meridian lines. Suitable for all levels, whether you are new to the practice or looking to deepen an existing engagement with it.</p>
</div>

<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Long-held postures, typically three to five minutes each</li>
<li>A focus on releasing deep connective tissue and opening the meridians</li>
<li>Guided breathwork and meditative elements throughout</li>
<li>A calm, supportive space for all levels</li>
<li>Regular monthly sessions delivered live online</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="reveal" id="10h-qigong-tcm">Qigong, Energy Cultivation and Relevant Aspects of TCM</h3>
<p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#5A9EAD;" class="reveal">A 10-hour module, taught standalone or within a Yoga Teacher Training</p>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>This focused 10-hour module introduces the principles of Qigong and the foundations of Traditional Chinese Medicine that directly relate to energy cultivation. It can be taken standalone or delivered as a module within a Yoga Teacher Training, and bridges two ancient Asian traditions that share a common concern: the cultivation, circulation and preservation of vital energy.</p>
</div>

<h4 class="reveal" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.4em;margin-bottom:0.4em;">Module Content</h4>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">Practice</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Thorough practice of an Active Qigong Five Element Control Cycle form, utilising Wuji and working across all meridians</li>
<li>Internal work: using the Yi (mind) to guide the energy</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">Foundations of Qigong and TCM</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Introduction to Qigong as a branch of Traditional Chinese Medicine</li>
<li>Qi and its relationship to the yogic concept of Prana</li>
<li>The Three Treasures (San Bao) and their correspondence with the Pancha Kosha model</li>
<li>The Three Dantian and their correspondence with key Chakra locations</li>
<li>The philosophical roots shared by Qigong and Yoga as contemplative energy practices</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">The Meridian System</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Structure and function of the Jing Luo (meridian and channel) system</li>
<li>The 12 primary meridians and their associated organ systems</li>
<li>The 8 extraordinary vessels, with particular focus on the Ren Mai and Du Mai</li>
<li>Comparison of the meridian system with the Nadi system in yogic anatomy</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">Acupoints</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>What acupoints (Xue Wei) are and how they function within the meridian system</li>
<li>Key acupoints relevant to Qigong self-cultivation and their locations</li>
<li>Categories of acupoints and their therapeutic significance</li>
<li>Comparison with the Marma points of Ayurveda and the Chakra system</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">Five Element Theory</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>The Wu Xing (Five Element) theory and its correspondences</li>
<li>The Sheng (generating) and Ke (controlling) cycles</li>
<li>Applying Five Element theory to Qigong practices and forms</li>
<li>Comparison of Wu Xing with the Pancha Mahabhuta (five great elements) of Yoga and Ayurveda</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.2em;margin-bottom:0.4em;" class="reveal">Integration with Yoga</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>How classical Qigong forms activate the meridian system and stimulate acupoints</li>
<li>Connections between Qigong meditation methods and the higher limbs of Raja Yoga (Pratyahara, Dharana, Dhyana)</li>
<li>An integrated view of Chinese and Indian energy systems for teaching</li>
<li>Ethical considerations when teaching across traditions</li>
</ul>

<h4 class="reveal" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15em;color:#2E5A6B;margin-top:1.4em;margin-bottom:0.4em;">Who Is This For</h4>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Trainee teachers on a 200-hour or 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training</li>
<li>Yoga practitioners who want to understand the energetic dimensions of their practice more deeply</li>
<li>Teachers looking to bridge yogic and Chinese traditions in their work</li>
</ul>

<p class="reveal">The module can be arranged standalone or delivered within an existing Yoga Teacher Training programme. Please register your interest below.</p>

<h3 class="reveal">Classes and Private Sessions</h3>

<p class="reveal">Therapeutic Yoga, Restorative Yoga, Vinyasa Yoga, Hatha Yoga and Yin Yoga, with Sound Healing integrated into sessions. Taught in Da Nang and online. Private sessions can focus on Yoga, Sound Healing, breathwork or a combination.</p>

<h3 class="reveal">Studio</h3>

<p class="reveal"><strong>Ngoc Han Studio</strong><br>Da Nang, Vietnam</p>
<p class="reveal">Some sessions are also held at ACE Hub, Da Nang, at other studios and venues, and outdoors at the beach (weather permitting).</p>

